  "chapter": {
    "number": 29,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(30) For the end, a Psalm",
          {
            "noteId": 53
          },
          "and Song at the dedication of the house of David."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will exalt you, O Lord; for you have lifted me up, and not caused my enemies to rejoice over me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O Lord my God, I cried to you, and you did heal me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O Lord, you have brought up my soul from Hades, you have delivered me from among them that go down to the pit.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Sing to the Lord, you⌃ his saints, and give thanks for the remembrance of his holiness.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For anger is in his wrath, but life in his favor: weeping shall wait for the evening, but joy shall be in the morning.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And I said in my prosperity, I shall never be moved.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O Lord, in your good pleasure you did add strength to my beauty: but you did turn away your face, and I was troubled.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "To you, O Lord, will I cry; and to my God will I make supplication.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "What profit is there in my blood, when I go down to destruction? Shall the dust give praise to you? or shall it declare your truth?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord heard, and had compassion upon me; the Lord is become my helper.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You have turned my mourning into joy for me: you have torn off my sackcloth, and girded me with gladness;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "that my glory may sing praise to you, and I may not be pierced with sorrow. O Lord my God, I will give thanks to you for ever.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 53,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. of a song.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 29,
          "verse": 0
        }
      }
    ]
